  <keyframe>
    <!-- Joint order: FL/FR/RL/RR x [hip, thigh, calf, wheel].  Angles taken from
         config/dhav1w.yaml.  Base heights are solved so the lowest collision
         geom sits exactly on z=0, accounting for the tilt the hip abduction puts
         on the wheels (a naive centre-minus-radius estimate is ~2 mm high for
         'stand' and ~8 mm high for 'sleep').  Note the config's stand pose is
         inherited from dhav1w and is nose-down: the rear thighs (0.87) sit the
         rear wheels 12 mm higher than the front (0.65).  See ../NOTES.md (I). -->
